SpamAgent 1.0

SpamAgent is a CGI-based mobile agent system to support evasive spamming
though mobile code.

A mobile agent is a program written in the Tcl language that can travel from
host to host to carry out its spamming task. The agent is represented by an
XML document that encapsulates the agent credentials, the agent code, and the
agent data.  

The migration mechanism relies on the existing Web infrastructure. That is,
in order to start its execution, an agent submits a POST request to the agent
system, which is a CGI program. 

The generic interpreter is extended with four application-specific commands,
namely data, results, store, and go. The "data" command is used to set and get
the contents of an agent's items. The "results" command is used to retrieve
and set the contents of the agent results. The "store" command is used to
permanently store data on the host's filesystem. Finally, the "go" command
allows an agent to dispatch a copy of itself to another server. The "go"
command takes, as a parameter, the URL that identifies another mobile agent
system (that is, another SpamAgent CGI script). When the "go" command is
executed by an agent, the agent system creates a new agent representation and
performs an HTTP POST request to that remote site.

The go command blocks until the POST command terminates and eventually returns
a result string. Note that this means that if an agents starts on host A and
performs a go to host B, the agent on host A will have to wait until the
"copy" on host B has finished before returning the results to whoever
dispatched the agent on host A. 
